    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside profile of **Junior Caminero** (69.89), whose matchup against a middle-of-the-road arm like Cabrera provides the optimal mix of talent and opportunity. While **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.93) boasts the highest raw score against Quantrill, the real value lies in **Casey Schmitt** (62.40). Despite a more modest base projection, **Schmitt** is a priority start today due to a rare confluence of a favorable 2-hole spot, a helpful wind blowing out, and a specific scouting edge against a slow-delivering pitcher that primes him for a crucial stolen base. **Colt Keith** (62.89) rounds out our elite tier, taking advantage of a weak matchup against Teng to solidify the heart of our production.\n\nWhile we remain aggressive in chasing volume, the decision to bench **Jacob Gonzalez** (47.60) was a tight call. He sits just outside our \"Strong\" tier; while he benefits from a generous matchup against Wacha, the bottom-of-the-order placement (8th) suppresses his run-scoring probability compared to the high-OBP roles occupied by **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**. We must also monitor **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (48.29) closely; while his speed is vital to our stolen base strategy, his score is severely hampered by a rough platoon matchup against Harrison, putting him near our efficiency floor. We are proceeding with this configuration to balance our pursuit of speed with the hard efficiency metrics required to maintain our position in the standings.",
